[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Concrete prompts & outcomes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Prompt**: “Write a multi-stage Dockerfile for a FastAPI app that runs as non-root and has a healthcheck.”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Result**: First draft left the final stage as root. I changed it to `USER 10001` and added an explicit non-root user creation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Prompt**: “Generate a least-privilege IAM policy for a service that only needs GetItem/Query/Scan on one DynamoDB table and GetSecretValue on one secret.”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Result**: AI initially produced `"Action": ["dynamodb:*"]` and `"Resource": "*"`. I rejected the wildcards and rewrote the policy with explicit actions and resource ARNs (see `terraform/main.tf`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Prompt**: “Create a GitHub Actions workflow that fails the build on critical Trivy findings and on any secret detected by Gitleaks.”[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Result**: Structure was correct, but the Trivy step originally used `exit-code: 0`. I set it to `1` so the job fails on CRITICAL.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Specific insecure AI default that was caught and fixed[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mClassic real-world failure mode: AI-generated Terraform IAM policy contained wildcard actions and resources (`"*"`).[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mCaught by reading the generated policy against the hard constraint “No IAM policy uses a wildcard … unless explicitly justified”.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mReplaced with the narrow, single-resource statements that appear in the final `main.tf`.[m
