[32m+[m[32m# Incident Runbook – Suspected Unauthorized Access to the Wallet Database[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Scenario**: Alert or log indicates possible unauthorized access to the DynamoDB wallets table.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Detection (0–5 min)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Confirm the alert source (Prometheus rule, log anomaly, or security tool).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Capture the exact time window, principal, and actions observed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Note any correlated spikes in `novapay_wallet_requests_total{status=~"5.."}`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Immediate containment (5–15 min)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Disable or revoke the compromised IAM role / temporary credentials.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Rotate the Secrets Manager secret:[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m   # LocalStack example[m
[32m+[m[32m   awslocal secretsmanager put-secret-value \[m
[32m+[m[32m     --secret-id novapay-wallet/db-credentials \[m
[32m+[m[32m     --secret-string '{"username":"novapay_app","password":"<new-random>"}'[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Force a new deployment of the wallet service so it reloads the secret.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. If a source IP is known, tighten the security-group ingress rules.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Investigation (15–60 min)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Snapshot the DynamoDB table for forensics.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Review access logs / CloudTrail equivalent for the window of compromise.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Identify which wallets (if any) were accessed and whether balances changed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Check whether any other secrets or roles were used by the same principal.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Eradication & recovery[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Confirm the root cause (compromised key, overly broad policy, etc.).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rotate all related credentials.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Re-enable the service with the new secret and tightened policies.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Verify `/health` and `/ready` return 200 and that metrics look normal.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Post-incident (within 24 h)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Update this runbook with any new lessons learned.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Add or tighten alerting rules if gaps were found.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Notify the compliance / CBN contact if personal data was exposed (NDPA 2023).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Schedule a blameless post-mortem.[m
